### Rotating Card (Hover‑to‑Flip) – Pure CSS

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a “card” that flips (rotates) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    margin:0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    width:260px;          /* card width */
    height:360px;         /* card height */
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card itself (the flipping element) ---------- */
.card {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
    transition:transform .6s ease;  /* smooth flip animation */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Hover trigger ---------- */
.card-wrapper:hover .card {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* rotate around Y axis */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* hide backside when flipped */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);       /* start rotated so it becomes visible after flip */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣ Sample content styling ---------- */
.card-front h2,
.card-back h2 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    font-size:1.4rem;
}
.card-front p,
.card-back p {
    margin:0;
    font-size:.95rem;
    color:#555;
}
```

</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front face -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>This is the front of the card.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back face -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>This is the back of the card.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

---

#### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` | Gives the 3D context so rotations look realistic. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on `.card` | Keeps child elements (`.card-face`) in 3D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility:hidden` on faces | Hides the backside of each face when it's turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | `transition: transform .6s ease` on `.card` | Smoothly animates the rotation. |
| **5** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Flips the card around the Y‑axis. |
| **6** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.card-back` | Positions the back face opposite the front so it appears when flipped. |

---

#### Customization tips

| Property | Where to change | Effect |
|----------|-----------------|--------|
| `width / height` | `.card-wrapper` | Size of the card. |
| `perspective` | `.card-wrapper` | Depth of the 3D effect (larger → flatter). |
| `transition` duration | `.card` | Speed of the flip. |
| `background` colors | `.card-front`, `.card-back` | Visual style. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | `.card` on hover | Change to `rotateX(180deg)` for vertical flip. |

Enjoy experimenting!
